# Files this fork owns outright. On a merge from upstream, keep our version and discard
# theirs rather than combining the two.
#
# Requires the driver to be registered once per clone, because git will not run a driver
# it has no definition for -- and says nothing when it skips one:
#
#     git config merge.ours.driver true
#
# `true` is the shell command /usr/bin/true: it exits 0 without writing to the working copy,
# which git reads as "the merge succeeded, the file on disk is the result".
#
# Caveat: this only engages when BOTH sides changed the file since the merge base. If our
# side never touches a file and upstream does, git takes upstream's copy without consulting
# any driver. That is fine for everything listed here, all of which we have already rewritten.
README.md merge=ours

# The app icon manifest. Ours is a single 1024 universal entry pointing at MiniStore.png;
# upstream's is 158 lines of per-size entries whose PNGs this fork deleted. A text merge
# would not just be unwanted, it would be broken - reinstating any of those entries points
# the asset catalog at files that are not in the tree.
AltStore/Resources/Icons.xcassets/AppIcon.appiconset/Contents.json merge=ours
